de343aff (541 1793254411616 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f371") (src . "init keeps an existing .gitignore and refuses one that is not a file\n\ninit wrote the store's .gitignore over whatever was there, so an existing\nfile lost its content, and a .gitignore that was a link was replaced (or a\ndirectory made init fail half-way). init now follows supply's rule: an\nexisting .gitignore keeps every byte, and only the store's lines it does\nnot hold as whole lines are appended, in the store's order, after a\nnewline when the file lacks a final one; a file that holds them all is not\nwritten. One carriage return at a line's end, before its newline or at\nthe end of the file, is set aside to compare, as git reads it; the bytes\nare written back unchanged. A .gitignore that is not a regular file (a\nlink, a directory, anything else) is refused before init writes anything,\nand so is one that cannot be read. The comment says what window remains\nbetween looking at the file and reading it.\n\n- store.sc: gitignore-after merges as bytes; store-init! classifies the\n  .gitignore once and refuses a non-regular or unreadable one first.\n- README: the init sentence says so.\n- Tests: store-in-git (kept lines, a full file untouched with its inode,\n  no file, no final newline, non-UTF-8, CRLF, a CR at the end, a double CR,\n  an empty file, a link, a directory, a FIFO, an unreadable file);\n  unreadable-census; rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 501))))
